IMPORT prelude

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, THE NOUNS.
-- DECLARE and nothing else: the choices of fact a person who knows the contract can state.  No rules.
-- The Act has no Parts and no Schedules; every module of layer 1 follows its sections.
--
-- The test for belonging here: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact, or does
-- answering it need the Act?  Only the first kind is here.  Whether the fact makes a right exist,
-- or bars one, is a rule and sits with the section that says so.

§ `Section 2 -- the third party's right`

-- How the third party is identified in the contract (s 2(3)): the three ways the Act lists, and the
-- two ways it does not.
DECLARE `Way the third party is identified in the contract` IS ONE OF
    `expressly, by name`
    `expressly, as a member of a class`
    `expressly, as answering a particular description`
    `by implication only`
    `not identified at all`

-- Whether a term of the contract excludes or limits liability (s 2(6)).
DECLARE `Kind of term` IS ONE OF
    `a term that excludes or limits liability in relation to a matter`
    `any other term`

-- What a reference in the Act to the third party "enforcing the term" is to be read as (s 2(6)).
DECLARE `Meaning of a reference to enforcing a term` IS ONE OF
    `enforcing the term`
    `availing of the exclusion or limitation`

-- Where a party stands to a term that a third party can enforce (s 2(7)).
DECLARE `Position of a party in relation to the term` IS ONE OF
    `the party by whom the term is enforceable against the promisor`
    `the party against whom the term is enforceable by the third party`
    `a party in neither of those positions`

§ `Section 3 -- varying and rescinding the contract`

-- What the parties to the contract do, by agreement, to the contract (s 3(1)).
DECLARE `What the parties do by agreement` IS ONE OF
    `rescind the contract`
    `vary the contract in such a way as to extinguish or alter the third party's entitlement`
    `vary the contract in some other way`
    `change the contract otherwise than by agreement of the parties`

-- The form of the third party's assent (s 3(2)(a)).
DECLARE `Form of the third party's assent` IS ONE OF
    `words`
    `conduct`
    `silence or inaction`
    `some other form`

-- An express term of the contract about the third party's consent (s 3(3)).
DECLARE `Express term of the contract about consent` IS ONE OF
    `a term under which the parties may rescind or vary without the third party's consent`
    `a term requiring the third party's consent in circumstances specified in the contract instead of those in section 3(1)(a), (b) and (c)`
    `no such express term`

-- The body that may dispense with a consent, or exercise the jurisdiction (s 3(4) to (7)).
DECLARE `Forum` IS ONE OF
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `a District Court`
    `another court`
    `an arbitral tribunal`

§ `Section 8 -- supplementary provisions`

-- How a third party might come to be treated as a party to the contract for another written law (s 8(4)).
DECLARE `Route by which the third party might be treated as a party` IS ONE OF
    `section 2(5)`
    `section 4(4)`
    `section 4(6)`
    `a provision other than section 2(5), 4(4) or 4(6)`

§ `Section 7 -- the carriage contracts`

-- What is carried, and by what mode, under a contract of carriage (s 7(5) and (6)).
-- The words of s 7(5)(b) and s 7(6) are "goods" for rail and road and "cargo" for air, so each of those three modes has
-- a choice for the carriage the words name and a choice for any other carriage by the same mode (passengers, say).
DECLARE `Mode of carriage` IS ONE OF
    `carriage by sea`
    `carriage of cargo by air`
    `carriage by air of something other than cargo, such as passengers`
    `carriage of goods by rail`
    `carriage by rail of something other than goods, such as passengers`
    `carriage of goods by road`
    `carriage by road of something other than goods, such as passengers`
    `carriage by some other mode`

-- The documents whose meaning s 7(7) hands to the Bills of Lading Act 1992.
DECLARE `Shipping document` IS ONE OF
    `a bill of lading`
    `a sea waybill`
    `a ship's delivery order`
    `any other document`

§ `Section 9 -- arbitration`

-- Which of the two Acts the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of (s 9).
DECLARE `Arbitration statute` IS ONE OF
    `the Arbitration Act 2001`
    `Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994`
    `neither of those`

-- Whether the matter asked about is a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the
-- enforcement of the substantive term by the third party (s 9(1)).
DECLARE `Dispute asked about` IS ONE OF
    `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party`
    `any other dispute`

-- When, relative to the third party's exercise of the right, the third party is asked about (s 9(2)).
DECLARE `Time asked about, relative to the exercise of the right` IS ONE OF
    `earlier than immediately before the exercise`
    `immediately before the exercise`
    `at or after the exercise`

§ `The parties and acts of the regulative rules`

-- The parties the Act directs: the parties to the contract (s 3(1)), the court or arbitral tribunal
-- (ss 3(4) to (6), 6) and the third party (s 4(6)).
DECLARE `Party under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the parties to the contract`
    `the court or arbitral tribunal`
    `the third party`

-- What the Act directs them to do or not do.
DECLARE `Act under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `rescind the contract by agreement without the third party's consent`
    `vary the contract by agreement without the third party's consent so as to extinguish or alter the third party's entitlement`
    `dispense with the third party's consent`
    `impose a condition on dispensing with the consent`
    `reduce the award to the third party`
    `enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party`
